# Accepted, time-boxed exceptions for the Trivy filesystem scan.

# CVE-2026-104851: fsspec < 2026.6.0, ReferenceFileSystem template rendering (HIGH).
# The lm-eval adapter pins fsspec 2025.3.0 because datasets==3.6.0 caps it at
# <=2025.3.0, and datasets>=4 cannot load the dataset-loading scripts that 7 of its
# 208 benchmarks need (cmmlu_*, aclue_*, ethics_cm, qasper_freeform). Nothing in the
# adapter, datasets, lm_eval or s3fs uses ReferenceFileSystem (grepped 2026-11-11),
# so the vulnerable code path is not reachable. See adapters/lm-eval/requirements.txt.
#
# The exception expires so it is re-evaluated. Remove it when lm-eval or the dataset
# owners make those tasks load without scripts and the adapter moves to datasets>=4.8.5
# (fsspec >= 2026.6.0). If that has not happened by the expiry date, drop the 7
# benchmarks and move to datasets>=4 instead of extending the exception. (The six
# pile_* benchmarks were dropped earlier for a different reason: their data host is
# gone, so they cannot run on any datasets version.)
CVE-2026-104851 exp:2027-01-31
